<!--
  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.Expressions
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation"
  xmlns:mapping="org.blockml.bml.mapping"
  xmlns:service="org.blockml.bml.service">

  <name>Expressions</name>
  <type>doc:Expressions</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to BlockML expressions</is>

  <documentation>
    The BML Expression Language is extended JSON inside ${ } delimiters. It appears wherever
    a Block member value needs to be dynamic — derived, computed, or bound to a service.

    Four additions beyond JSON:
    • Property references — myProp, myProp.x (StructType members by name only; no size[0])
    • Model bindings — @model:/path, @model:relativeAttr
    • Bean calls — @bean.capa(...), @bean.capa (linking when no parentheses)
    • Built-in calls — #math.min(a, b), #strings.trim(s)

    Expression vs BOM data layer (separate layers):
    • BOM stores LiteralValue and ExpressionValue.raw — immutable, authored form
    • parseExpression() produces AST and type inference — utility output, not BOM mutation
    • evaluateExpression() resolves values — renderer working model only

    The Validator checks expression correctness (referenced members, visibility, types,
    valid capabilities) but never executes expressions. Evaluation belongs exclusively to
    the Renderer (Stage 3).

    Bean calls resolve context-scoped beans declared as Aggregations with beanName. Capability
    call argument mapping uses FunctionMapping — positional order follows inputType field
    declaration order. Named and positional arguments must not be mixed in one call.

    Model bindings use @model: with : separator. Absolute paths start with /; relative paths
    resolve against the binding context of the nearest parent Model-bound Aggregation.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see file="10_expression_language.md" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Authoritative expression language reference — grammar, AST, bean calls, bindings.
    </see>
    <see file="01_bom_core.md" relation="DeepDive">
